# What the build may see. An allowlist, not a list of exclusions: the image's
# contents are a promise this project makes (`openspec/specs/deployment`), and a
# denylist keeps that promise only until somebody adds a directory.
#
# The two that matter most if this is ever loosened: `.data/` holds the model
# weights (2.8 GB) and the demo corpus, and `.git/` holds every version of
# everything. Neither belongs in a build context, let alone in an image.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!alembic.ini
!alembic/
!app/
!ui/

# Re-excluded inside the directories above: nothing a build produces.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
